WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.900
Complete coverage index, part three.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:08.100
The final stretch: tooling, operations, safety, governance, and what's emerging.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:14.202
Hugging Face Transformers is the model library everything else plugs into,

4
00:00:14.202 --> 00:00:19.833
and Firefly and Llama-Factory are config-driven fine-tuning suites alongside Axolotl.

5
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.857
Then there are four ways to split a model across GPUs.

6
00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.167
Tensor parallelism.

7
00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:26.867
Pipeline parallelism.

8
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.533
Sequence parallelism.

9
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:29.967
And model sharding.

10
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:34.633
Weights and Biases and Neptune handle experiment tracking.

11
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:41.767
Metaflow, from Netflix, and ZenML are pipeline frameworks, and Azure ML is Microsoft's platform.

12
00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.360
Auto-scaling adds replicas on load.

13
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.833
It's the Kubernetes primitive behind elastic serving.

14
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:53.722
These are commercial model and LLM monitoring vendors: WhyLabs,

15
00:00:53.722 --> 00:00:58.633
Fiddler, and Datadog AI Monitoring, alongside Arize and Evidently.

16
00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:03.300
What they all watch is cost tracking, token usage, latency, and drift.

17
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.133
Safety operations put checks at every boundary.

18
00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.800
Input validation checks what comes in.

19
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:15.100
Detectors, classifiers or judges, flag jailbreaks, hallucinations, and bias.

20
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.007
Output filtering checks what goes out,

21
00:01:18.007 --> 00:01:23.701
and output sanitization strips unsafe content, like scripts or PII, before display.

22
00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:27.200
Adversarial testing deliberately tries to break it.

23
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.700
Guardrail tooling enforces shape, either while decoding or by validating afterwards.

24
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.232
Structured generation and regex constraints work at decode time,

25
00:01:38.232 --> 00:01:42.133
and LMQL and Guidance are constrained-generation languages.

26
00:01:42.433 --> 00:01:45.771
JSON schema validation works at validation time.

27
00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.900
Prompt Armor is an injection-defense product.

28
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.300
Governance has its own vocabulary.

29
00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:58.200
Responsible AI is the umbrella program, and AI ethics is the field these sit inside.

30
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.367
Explainable AI makes decisions inspectable,

31
00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:06.900
for example by attention visualization, showing which tokens the model attended to.

32
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.933
Model cards and data sheets are standardized documentation for models and datasets.

33
00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:18.867
ISO IEC 42001 is a certifiable AI management standard.

34
00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:23.600
And data anonymization irreversibly removes identity from records.

35
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.200
A few infrastructure names for the full-stack vocabulary.

36
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.933
MongoDB and NoSQL are document stores for flexible schemas.

37
00:02:33.233 --> 00:02:38.067
Ansible is configuration management, as opposed to Terraform's provisioning.

38
00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:41.387
And a CDN is edge caching for static assets.

39
00:02:41.387 --> 00:02:46.467
Add Postgres and Redis, and that's the storage vocabulary of a full stack.

40
00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:51.900
This is the discipline that decides whether a model learns or memorizes.

41
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.733
You start with a corpus, then deduplicate it.

42
00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:57.100
Then label or annotate the data.

43
00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.677
And split it into train, validation, and test sets.

44
00:03:00.677 --> 00:03:05.367
Curriculum learning adds one more idea: order the data from easy to hard.

45
00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:10.100
Slow thinking is the System 2 framing of reasoning models.

46
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:16.721
Browser use, multi-modal agents, and audio agents act over the web, mixed media, and voice.

47
00:03:16.721 --> 00:03:21.167
Real-time AI means sub-second systems like voice and live video.

48
00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:28.267
Speculative editing adapts speculative decoding to rewriting existing text, used in fast code edits.

49
00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:30.351
Let's recap.

50
00:03:30.351 --> 00:03:34.033
Parallelism and sharding split models across GPUs.

51
00:03:34.333 --> 00:03:37.767
Monitoring watches cost, tokens, latency, and drift.

52
00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:42.000
Safety checks both boundaries, and governance documents the system.

53
00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.400
And data discipline decides whether a model learns or memorizes.
